preload-google-drive-help = Enables a recursive Google Drive VFS directory-cache refresh in the background after mounting. File contents are not downloaded.
preload-onedrive-help = Enables a directory-only OneDrive walk in the background after mounting so folders open faster. File contents are not downloaded.
preload-box-help = Enables a depth-limited Box directory walk in the background after mounting. The depth limit reduces API requests and the risk of Box rate limiting.
preload-sharepoint-help = Optionally walks directories in the selected SharePoint library or folder after mounting. Off by default; keep the time and depth small to limit Microsoft requests. File contents are not downloaded.
preload-smb-help = Enables a depth-limited SMB directory walk in the background after network and VPN readiness. Individual SMB connections may override this global policy.
preload-smb-global = Use global SMB preload settings
rclone-detect = Detect rclone remotes
rclone-detect-help = Read rclone config dump, filter remotes by provider backend, and offer matching remotes as selectable account choices. If no { $provider } remotes are detected, enter an existing remote name or create one here.
rclone-detected-remotes = Detected { $provider } rclone remotes:
rclone-use-remote-help = Use rclone remote `{ $name }` with backend `{ $backend }` for this connection.
rclone-manage-remotes = Manage unused rclone remotes:
rclone-remote-in-use = In use
rclone-remote-removing = Removing...
rclone-remote-confirm-remove = Confirm Remove
rclone-remote-remove = Remove remote
rclone-remote-in-use-help = rclone remote `{ $name }` is referenced by a saved connection and cannot be removed here.
rclone-remote-remove-help = Remove rclone remote `{ $name }` from rclone configuration. This does not remove applet connections, local data, or cloud files.

rclone-remote-directory = optional remote subtree/folder
rclone-remote-directory-help = Leave empty for the whole rclone remote, or enter an existing folder/subtree to limit this connection.
onedrive-account-online = onedriver account/setup reference
onedrive-account-offline = onedrive account/setup reference
onedrive-account-online-help = Label this OneDrive Online Mount account so you can recognize it later, for example `onedriver-work`. Test Connection and Save validate jstaf/onedriver, app-owned auth metadata, mountpoint safety, and active onedriver overlaps without reading provider tokens.
onedrive-account-offline-help = Label this OneDrive Offline Mirror account so you can recognize it later, for example `onedrive-personal`. Test Connection and Save validate auth metadata, directory safety, active onedriver overlap, and a bounded dry-run preview.
onedrive-account-online-warning = Do not reuse this mountpoint for a OneDrive mirror.
onedrive-account-offline-warning = Do not reuse this mirror directory for a OneDrive Online mount.
onedrive-folder = optional OneDrive folder/subtree
onedrive-folder-help = Leave empty for the whole OneDrive account, or enter an existing folder/subtree to limit this connection.
onedrive-setup-online = Start OneDrive Setup
onedrive-setup-offline = Start OneDrive Mirror Setup
onedrive-setup-online-help = Complete all required fields before setup, then finish onedriver authorization in the browser. After authorization, run Test Connection and Save Connection.
onedrive-setup-offline-help = Complete all required fields before setup, then finish OneDrive authorization in the browser. After browser authorization, Cloud Mounter waits for onedrive and runs dry-run validation; this can take several minutes. Save reuses that validation if the form is unchanged.
onedrive-auth-manual = Use Manual Auth Handoff
onedrive-auth-manual-help = Fallback for browser or tenant cases where onedrive cannot capture the redirect automatically. The applet prepares auth-files and a response URL field.
onedrive-auth-prompt = Press Start OneDrive Mirror Setup to prepare the auth URL handoff files.
onedrive-auth-title = OneDrive mirror authentication handoff
onedrive-auth-intro = After pressing Start OneDrive Mirror Setup, wait a moment for onedrive to create the auth URL, then open it in your browser:
onedrive-auth-open = Open OneDrive Auth Helper
onedrive-auth-open-help = Open the generated onedrive auth URL in the WebKitGTK helper when available. The helper attempts to capture the final Microsoft redirect automatically; otherwise the applet falls back to xdg-open.
onedrive-auth-shell-fallback = Shell fallback:
onedrive-auth-shell-command = shell command
onedrive-auth-shell-help = This selectable command opens the same auth URL in your normal browser if the WebKitGTK helper cannot be used.
onedrive-auth-redirect-intro = After Microsoft redirects to the native-client page, paste the full browser address-bar URL below. The applet writes it to the transient response file for onedrive and does not save it in configuration.
onedrive-auth-redirect = paste full Microsoft redirect URL
onedrive-auth-redirect-help = Paste the full URL beginning with https://login.microsoftonline.com/... and containing code=.
onedrive-auth-submit = Submit OneDrive Response URL
onedrive-auth-submit-help = Write the pasted response URL to the transient response file expected by the running onedrive authentication process.

google-drive-remote-name = Google Drive rclone remote name
google-drive-remote-help-add = Enter a new rclone remote name, such as `personal_gdrive`, optionally enter its matching custom OAuth client ID and secret, then click Create Google Drive Remote. To use an existing remote, select a detected Google Drive remote or enter its exact name from `rclone config`. The applet verifies backend type `drive`, authentication, and subtree access before saving.
google-drive-remote-help-modify = Select a detected Google Drive remote or enter its exact name from `rclone config`. To replace its OAuth client, enter the matching client ID and secret and click Update Google OAuth Client; this repeats browser authorization. The applet verifies backend type `drive`, authentication, and subtree access before saving.
google-drive-create = Create Google Drive Remote
google-drive-create-help = Create the rclone Google Drive remote with full-drive scope and local browser OAuth. A custom client ID requires its matching client secret. Complete browser authorization, then run Test Connection. OAuth values stay in rclone config, not applet configuration.
google-drive-update = Update Google OAuth Client
google-drive-update-help = Explicitly replace this rclone remote's Google OAuth client ID and secret and authorize it again in the browser. Both fields are required. Remount active connections afterward.
google-drive-client-id = Google OAuth client ID
google-drive-client-id-help = Use the OAuth client ID from a Google Cloud Desktop app with the Google Drive API enabled. Rclone says a private client is required to avoid interruption during its 2026 shared-client retirement. Leaving both OAuth fields blank attempts the shared client only for compatibility.
google-drive-client-secret = Google OAuth client secret
google-drive-client-secret-warning = The applet does not save this value in its configuration or logs.
google-drive-client-secret-help = Enter the secret issued with the client ID. Client ID and secret must be supplied together. The value is passed directly to rclone and cleared from this form after the operation.

box-remote-name = Box rclone remote name
box-remote-help-add = Enter a new rclone remote name, such as `box_personal`, then click Create Box Remote. To use an existing remote, select a detected Box remote or enter its exact name from `rclone config`. The applet verifies backend type `box`, authentication, and subtree access before saving.
box-remote-help-modify = Select a detected Box remote or enter its exact name from `rclone config`. The applet verifies backend type `box`, authentication, and subtree access before saving.
box-create = Create Box Remote
box-create-help = Create the rclone Box remote with local browser OAuth. Complete the browser authorization window that rclone opens, then run Test Connection. Credentials and refresh tokens stay in rclone config, not applet configuration.

smb-remote-name = SMB rclone remote name
smb-remote-help-add = Enter a new rclone remote name, such as `office_smb`, then fill in the SMB settings and click Create/Update SMB Remote. To use an existing remote, select a detected SMB remote or enter its exact name from `rclone config`. Create/Update SMB Remote can also update that remote. The applet verifies backend type `smb`. Passwords stay in rclone, not applet configuration.
smb-remote-help-modify = Select a detected SMB remote or enter its exact name from `rclone config`. The applet verifies backend type `smb` and share access before saving. Credentials remain in rclone configuration.
smb-create-update = Create/Update SMB Remote
smb-create-update-help = Create or update the rclone SMB remote with host/user/domain metadata. If the SMB password field is filled, the applet updates the rclone password and then clears the field. Passwords stay in rclone, not applet configuration.
smb-update = Update SMB Remote
smb-update-help = Update the selected rclone SMB remote. Enter a password to rotate it without saving the password in applet configuration; host, username, and domain are optional for existing remotes.
smb-host = SMB server host
smb-host-help = Server DNS name or IP address used for rclone's SMB `host` option. Create/Update SMB Remote uses these fields and leaves passwords in rclone, not applet configuration.
smb-username = SMB username
smb-username-help = Optional SMB username. Leave blank for guest or rclone defaults.
smb-domain = SMB domain or WORKGROUP
smb-domain-help = Optional NTLM domain. WORKGROUP is rclone's default.
smb-password = SMB password (leave blank to keep existing)
smb-password-warning = The applet does not save this password.
smb-password-help = Enter a password only when creating a new SMB remote or changing an expired/incorrect SMB password. On success it is stored in rclone's config and cleared from this form.

sftp-provider = SFTP
sftp-remote-name = SFTP rclone remote name
sftp-remote-help-add = Enter a new remote name and SFTP settings, then Create/Update SFTP Remote, or select an existing SFTP remote. Passwords and keys remain with rclone or your SSH agent.
sftp-remote-help-modify = Select an existing SFTP remote. Update SFTP Remote explicitly changes server settings or credentials; Test and Save only use the existing remote.
sftp-action-applying = Applying SFTP Remote…
sftp-action-confirm = Confirm SFTP Update
sftp-action-create-update = Create/Update SFTP Remote
sftp-action-update = Update SFTP Remote
sftp-action-help = Explicitly save server settings and authentication in rclone. Blank secrets retain existing values for the same authentication method. Restart active connections using the updated remote.
sftp-host = SFTP server host
sftp-host-help = Server DNS name or IP address; do not include sftp:// or a directory.
sftp-port = SSH port (22)
sftp-port-help = SSH port from 1 to 65535. The default is 22.
sftp-username = SFTP username
sftp-username-help = Account on the SFTP server.
sftp-auth-password = Password
sftp-auth-password-help = Use the remote account's login password. The server must allow password authentication. Enter it below; blank keeps an existing password when updating the same authentication method.
sftp-auth-key = SSH Key
sftp-auth-key-help = Use a local private-key file, not its .pub file. The matching public key must be authorized on the server. Encrypted OpenSSH keys require SSH Agent; supported encrypted PEM keys can use the passphrase field below.
sftp-auth-agent = SSH Agent
sftp-auth-agent-help = Use a key already unlocked in your SSH agent. Run ssh-add -l to list keys, or ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 to load one. The applet's host user service also needs access to that agent through SSH_AUTH_SOCK.
sftp-password = Password (blank keeps existing)
sftp-password-help = Required for a new password login. Blank keeps the existing password on update. The applet clears this field after setup and never saves it in its own configuration.
sftp-key-file = Private-key file on host
sftp-key-file-help = Absolute host path or ~/. Encrypted OpenSSH keys require SSH agent authentication; direct passphrases support rclone-compatible encrypted PEM keys.
sftp-key-passphrase = Key passphrase (blank keeps existing for same key)
sftp-key-passphrase-help = Leave blank for an unencrypted key. To unlock an encrypted OpenSSH key, use your SSH agent instead. Passphrases remain with rclone.
sftp-agent-summary = Use an unlocked key from your SSH agent.
sftp-agent-summary-help = The host user service must be able to access SSH_AUTH_SOCK. A key available only in a terminal may not be available to a login service.
sftp-known-hosts = Known-hosts file on host
sftp-known-hosts-help = Use a verified SSH known_hosts file, normally ~/.ssh/known_hosts. Unknown or changed host keys stop the connection; the applet does not add or replace keys.
sftp-remote-directory = optional SFTP remote directory
sftp-remote-directory-help = Leave empty for the login directory. Relative paths start there; / starts at the server filesystem root permitted to your account.
sftp-preload-global = Use global SFTP preload settings
sftp-preload-help = Optional depth-limited SFTP directory preload. Off by default, 30 seconds, depth 2. Skips /proc, /sys, and /dev on server-root mounts and never follows symbolic links. Each connection may override these defaults.
sftp-host-label = host
sftp-user-label = username
sftp-private-key-label = private-key file
sftp-known-hosts-label = known-hosts file
sftp-required = SFTP { $field } is required.
sftp-host-invalid = SFTP host must be a DNS name or IP address, without a URL or directory.
sftp-port-invalid = SFTP port must be between 1 and 65535.
sftp-path-invalid = SFTP { $field } must be an absolute host path or start with ~/.
sftp-config-parse = Could not parse rclone configuration.
sftp-config-invalid = Invalid rclone configuration.
sftp-wrong-provider = This remote belongs to another provider. Choose an SFTP remote or a new name.
sftp-config-read = Could not read host rclone configuration.
sftp-settings-loaded = SFTP server settings loaded. Secrets remain blank; Update SFTP Remote explicitly applies changes.
sftp-remote-not-found-help = SFTP remote was not found. Select an existing remote or create one in Add Connection.
sftp-reenter-secret = The previous SFTP update failed. Re-enter the password or key passphrase before retrying.
sftp-update-affects = Updating this remote affects: { $connections }. Restart active connections afterward. Click Confirm SFTP Update to apply these settings.
sftp-applying = Applying SFTP remote `{ $name }`…
sftp-invalid-config-request = Invalid configuration request.
sftp-remote-gone = Remote no longer exists. Create it in Add Connection first.
sftp-save-failed = SFTP save remote failed. Check rclone configuration permissions and inspect the remote before retrying; settings may have changed.
sftp-unexpected-response = Rclone returned an unexpected setup response; inspect the remote before retrying.
sftp-needs-configuration = Rclone setup needs additional configuration. Complete it with rclone config and then select the remote.
sftp-stage-timeout = SFTP { $stage } timed out after { $seconds } seconds. Inspect the remote before retrying; settings may have changed.
sftp-rclone-missing = rclone is missing on the host.
sftp-stage-cancelled = SFTP { $stage } was cancelled.
sftp-invalid-option = SFTP setup contains an invalid option.
sftp-start-failed = Could not start host rclone for SFTP setup.
sftp-stage-failed = SFTP { $stage } failed. Check rclone configuration permissions and inspect the remote before retrying; settings may have changed.
sftp-backend-mismatch = Remote backend is not SFTP.
sftp-custom-ssh = This remote uses custom SSH commands or an embedded key. Manage its authentication with rclone config. Applet access testing requires rclone's built-in SSH authentication.
sftp-password-required = Enter a password for a new password login.
sftp-invalid-remote-name = Invalid remote name.
sftp-invalid-backend = Invalid backend.
sftp-invalid-request = Invalid SFTP request.
sftp-host-verification-read = Could not read SFTP host-verification settings.
sftp-remote-not-found = SFTP remote was not found.
sftp-external-ssh = This remote uses an external SSH command. Select a remote using rclone's built-in SFTP authentication so the applet can verify its host-key policy.
sftp-known-hosts-required = SFTP requires a known-hosts file. Set a verified file with Create/Update SFTP Remote before testing or saving.
sftp-stage-read-config = read configuration
sftp-stage-save-remote = save remote

